# Netlify-style redirects for /blogs/<slug>
# NOTE: This file is for Netlify (and similar hosts) only. Vercel reads vercel.json — keep them in sync.
# This file is read by Netlify (and similar hosts) at deploy time.
#
# HONEST CAVEAT (2026-08-27):
# The export on disk only contains the blog LIST page (blogs/index.html) plus
# the JS bundles and CMS data. It does NOT contain per-blog HTML pages like
# /blogs/<slug>/index.html — those are missing because the extraction tool did
# not capture them.
#
# A redirect alone CANNOT render a single blog post — when the user lands on
# /blogs/<slug>, the browser must receive an HTML file that:
#   1. Sets `data-framer-hydrate-v2` routeId to the blog-DETAIL routeId
#      (currently unknown to us; case-studies detail uses routeId `vS7puIghp`)
#   2. Sets pathVariables = {<blog-binding>: <slug>}
#   3. Pre-renders the blog content via hydration
#
# What this redirect does (best-effort without a per-blog HTML file):
# - Sends /blogs/<slug> -> /blogs/?slug=<slug>
# - The list page will still render, not the single blog.
# - It is a graceful "no 404" fallback, NOT a fix.
#
# The proper fix is to ask the Framer project's owner to re-export with
# "Static HTML" enabled so each blog post becomes a real file.

